body:
The design review explicitly agreed on alphabetical tie-break for equal remainders in percent_shares:
  percent_shares({"web": 1, "api": 1, "db": 1}) == {"web": 33, "api": 34, "db": 33}

However, the merged implementation (METRICORE-108) uses insertion-order tie-break, which produces:
  percent_shares({"web": 1, "api": 1, "db": 1}) == {"web": 34, "api": 33, "db": 33}

This contradicts the design review decision documented in handover notes. The sort key should use alphabetical order (sorted key name) instead of insertion order (enumerate index).

Fix: Change the tie-break in the sort from `order[item[1]]` (insertion index) to `item[1]` (key name for alphabetical sort).

